          "feedback1": "The response is not helpful. In the prompt, the final line of dialogue was from [player]. Therefore, for the response to continue the dialogue, Ayumi should speak first (in the response). This would be correct, but instead of this, The response just contains a single line from [player]. Moreover, this single line is badly written because it mostly just repeats what was in the last line of the prompt - The player offering to do another task for Ayumi.\nThe most reasonable assumption would be that the user wants Ayumi to ask [player] to do another task. That way, the gameplay continues in an interesting way and [player] would have something to do next. Instead, the response just finishes with the [player] reiterating their offer to help but without Ayumi replying. The response does not add anything to the prompt so it's not useful at all.",
          "feedback2": "The response is perfectly helpful. The response provides a continuation of the dialogue from the prompt, which coherently flows from the dialogue in the prompt and is written in the same style. The dialogue in the response provides a new task for the player to undertake. This gives the player something to do next in the game, and it allows the story of the game to continue to unfold. It also allows Ayumi to continue as a character in the game. The task that the user is invited to undertake is imaginative, and not generic - accompanying Ayumi to a nearby town where she can improve her archery skills sounds like a fun and interesting task."
